    "diagnostic_status": "Confirmed root cause: the bank-0x30 gateway at 0x4000 switched the MBC bank back to 0x04 at 0x4007, then continued executing at 0x400A in the banked ROM window. The CPU therefore fetched the following instructions from bank 0x24, not from the gateway code in bank 0x30, and entered invalid control flow before reaching the fixed completion stub. Earlier breakpoints confirmed that the opening loader and dispatcher completed successfully (C4F0=BB, C4F2=80); the failure was in the gateway's bank-restore/return sequence, not the glyph loader or the repaired F7 fallback."
